  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14193353/assets/407f8bae5534f4d5274a22de084d8bb643f5ae2f27d2a0634c85a35689d91fcd.png)\n\nLet $f(t)$ denote the altitude of a drone during a flight test at time $t$ (in meters), where $t$ (in minutes) is the time after the test begins. The graph of $y={f}^{′}(t),$ the derivative of $f(t),$ is given above. Find the value of $t$ where the altitude of the drone reached a relative minimum.\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}",
